\title{Support Ticket: Technical Issue with Third-Party API Integration}
\author{Your Name}
\date{\today}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\section*{Description of the Issue}
We have encountered a technical issue during the integration of a third-party API into our multi-tiered system architecture. The error occurs when attempting to make a request to the API using our application's frontend.

\subsection*{Error Message}
The following error message is displayed in the browser console:

\verb|Error: Network Error at new XMLHttpRequest(<anonymous>): "Failed to load" : net::ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED|

\subsection*{Logs and Screenshots}
Attached please find the relevant logs from our application server (see file "api\_integration\_logs.txt") and a screenshot of the error message (see file "error\_screenshot.png").

\section*{Proposed Solution}
Based on our initial investigation, it appears that the issue may be related to DNS resolution for the API endpoint. We propose the following solutions:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item Check DNS records for the API domain name and ensure they are correctly configured.
  \item Configure our application to use a specific DNS server for API requests.
  \item Implement a fallback mechanism for API requests, such as retrying with a different endpoint or using a cached response.
\end{enumerate}

\section*{Timeline for Resolution}
We estimate that implementing the proposed solutions will take approximately 2 business days. However, the actual resolution time may vary depending on the complexity of the issue and the availability of necessary resources.

\section*{Root Cause Analysis}
The root cause of this issue could be one or more of the following:

