2. Create a new file `Toast.js`:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { useContext } from 'react';
import { ToastContext } from './ToastContext';

const Toast = () => {
  const { children } = useContext(ToastContext);

  return <div id="toast" className="toast-container">{children}</div>;
};

export default Toast;
```

3. Use the `ToastProvider` and `Toast` components in your main app component:

```javascript
// App.js
import React from 'react';
import { ToastProvider, Toast } from './path/to/your/components';

function App() {
  return (
    <ToastProvider>
      <Toast>
        {/* Add your toast content here */}
        <p data-testid="toast">This is a test toast message!</p>
      </Toast>
      <YourMainContent />
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

Now you have created a simple toast notification system using React and context. To add more functionality like displaying multiple toasts or handling their dismissal, you can modify the `ToastProvider` implementation accordingly.

Keep in mind that this example does not include actual toast display logic. It only sets up the foundation for creating a custom toast solution using React context.

